    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-21207: y'(t)=2t vanishes at t=0 while x'(0)=2 is nonzero, giving a horizontal tangent and vertical normal. q-15805: substitution gives (x+4)(x-2)=0; the line then gives points (-4,-2) and (2,0). q-117247: substitution gives (x+1)(x-2)=0, yielding (-1,1) and (2,2). q-117542: substitution gives (x+3)^2=0, and y=-2. q-117546: substitution gives (x+3)^2=0, so x=-3. q-54242: the intersection quadratic is 2x^2-4x+5=0, with discriminant -24, so there are no real intersections. q-117737: the quadratic is (5/4)x^2-2x+3=0, with discriminant -11, so there are no real intersections. q-117859: the diameter endpoints are (8,0) and (0,-12); their midpoint is (4,-6), and the squared radius is 52. q-78784: endpoints (2,0) and (0,2) give center (1,1) and squared radius 2. q-7632: completing squares gives 5(x-1)^2+9(y-2)^2=45, hence center (1,2). q-7639: the standard form has denominators 8 and 4, hence center (1,-3), major-axis length 4\\sqrt{2}, and minor-axis length 4; only I and III are true. q-16565: the standard-form denominators are 16 and 4, so the major-axis length is 8. q-16561: the denominators are 4 and 25, so the minor-axis length is 4. q-3397 and q-15422: differentiating the selected antiderivatives returns the respective integrands; their coefficients also follow from integration by parts twice. q-125926: subtracting the logarithm series gives coefficients 1+4=5, -1/2+8=15/2, and 1/3+64/3=65/3. Exact current choice values and option tokens are preserved below.",
